1
00:00:00,349 --> 00:00:03,229
(Raj:)I can and I did.
Look up "dibs" in Wikipedia.

2
00:00:04,227 --> 00:00:05,937
(Sheldon:)Dibs doesn't apply in a bidding war.

3
00:00:06,104 --> 00:00:09,854
(Leonard:)It's not a bidding war. I'm selling it all
to Larry down at the comic-book store.

4
00:00:10,025 --> 00:00:12,985
- Why Larry? Did Larry call dibs?
- Will you forget dibs?

5
00:00:13,153 --> 00:00:15,533
(Leonard:)He offered me a fair price
for the whole collection.

6
00:00:15,697 --> 00:00:19,997
- What's the number? I'll match it.
- I'll match it, plus 1000 rupees.

7
00:00:20,160 --> 00:00:23,830
- What's the exchange rate?
- None of your business. Take it or leave it.

8
00:00:23,997 --> 00:00:26,537
Mom, my bar mitzvah bonds,
how much do I got?

9
00:00:26,708 --> 00:00:30,668
Thanks. I can go $2600
and two trees in Israel.

10
00:00:32,422 --> 00:00:36,262
(Leonard:)Forget it. Guys, if I sell to one of you,
the other two are gonna be mad at me.

11
00:00:36,426 --> 00:00:39,386
Who cares? As long as you pick me.

12
00:00:39,554 --> 00:00:41,644
(Raj:)Okay, Leonard, put down the box.
Let's talk.

13
00:00:41,807 --> 00:00:43,977
(Leonard:)Sorry, Raj, my mind is made up.

14
00:00:44,142 --> 00:00:47,392
(Sheldon(moving to block his path):)No. I can't let you do this.

15
00:00:47,562 --> 00:00:50,692
(Leonard:)Sheldon, get out of my way.

16
00:00:52,985 --> 00:00:55,695
(Sheldon(brandishing toy sword from Leonard's box):)None shall pass.

17
00:00:58,865 --> 00:01:00,245
(Penny:)Okay.

